{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,19]],"date-time":"2026-05-19T15:24:20Z","timestamp":1779204260797,"version":"3.51.4"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Project MUSE","issue":"3","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["ajm"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2006,6]]},"abstract":"<jats:p xml:lang=\"en\"> We consider minimal compact complex surfaces S with Betti numbers b 1 = 1 and n = b 2 &gt; 0. A theorem of Donaldson gives n exceptional line bundles. We prove that if in a deformation, these line bundles have sections, S is a degeneration of blown-up Hopf surfaces. Besides, if there exists an integer m \u2265 1 and a flat line bundle F such that H 0 ( S,-mK \u2297 F ) \u2260 0, then S contains a Global Spherical Shell. We apply this last result to complete classification of bihermitian surfaces.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1353\/ajm.2006.0021","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2006,5,28]],"date-time":"2006-05-28T13:23:07Z","timestamp":1148822587000},"page":"639-670","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":20,"title":["On surfaces of class VII + 0 with numerically anticanonical divisor"],"prefix":"10.1353","volume":"128","author":[{"given":"Georges","family":"Dloussky","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"147","container-title":["American Journal of Mathematics"],"original-title":[],"language":"en","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,20]],"date-time":"2024-01-20T00:26:54Z","timestamp":1705710414000},"score":1,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/muse.jhu.edu\/article\/198269"}},"subtitle":[],"short-title":[],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2006,6]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"3","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2006,6]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1353\/ajm.2006.0021","relation":{},"ISSN":["1080-6377"],"issn-type":[{"value":"1080-6377","type":"electronic